  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd an enabled Donate button at the right of the top bar.\nThe button uses the Tabler heart icon and the project Stripe link.\nThe code stores the link in one constant.\nThe native build opens the system browser on a background thread.\nA launch failure shows a message with the link in the status strip.\nThe browser build opens a new tab.\nThe action does not change the document or its history.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2a6f35687ad65eb4b54f1e09dfd25d3ef49e9e1a/issue-2385/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![After](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2a6f35687ad65eb4b54f1e09dfd25d3ef49e9e1a/issue-2385/after.png)\n\nThe images are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe top bar had no control for the funding link published in README.md and FUNDING.yml.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll eight Donate tests pass in the default UI library suite.\n\n- `donate_button_is_named_and_enabled_in_both_shells`\n- `donate_in_browser_opens_stripe_in_a_new_tab_without_a_document_edit`\n- `donate_browser_failure_is_named_and_recovery_does_not_edit_the_document`\n- `donate_link_matches_the_published_project_funding_link`\n- `layout_donate_top_right`\n- `donate_launcher_refuses_a_missing_executable`\n- `donate_launcher_reports_a_nonzero_exit`\n- `donate_launcher_accepts_a_successful_exit`\n\nThe label pin failed on unchanged upstream/main 3e47b898b before the fix.\nThe failure text is saved outside the branch.\nRestoring upstream/main's panes.rs made the label pin fail again.\nRestoring the fix made the pin pass.\nIgnoring a nonzero launcher exit made its pin fail.\nSuppressing a missing executable error made its pin fail.\nSuppressing the native failure message made its pin fail.\nEach pin passed after the correct code was restored.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 9 steps.\nThe gate passed 1,095 tests and ignored six existing tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe before and after images use the same real shell test harness.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff for `*.nc` and `*.cl` is empty.\nNo snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe tests do not open a real browser or submit a payment.\nThey use the test executable to check launcher success and failure.\nThe tests inject a native result to check the visible message.\nThread creation failure was not forced.\nWindows and macOS launchers were not run.\nThe wasm target is not installed, so wasm compilation was not checked.\nThe browser shell mode and its new-tab request were checked in the harness.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1798 changes `panes::status`, another icon row, other module declarations, and `assert_shell_skeleton`.\nThis PR changes `panes::ribbon` and adds separate declarations and tests.\nPRs #2185, #1330, and #1209 add other module declarations in mod.rs.\nPR #1687 adds another test module at the end of structural.rs.\nPR #2122 adds a different licence section in LICENSES.md.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nNo PR changes the function or lines used by this fix.\n\nEffort: low\n\nChangelog: Add a Donate button in the top bar that opens the project funding link and reports native browser launch failures.\n\nFixes #2385\n",
